### SecurePay — Stripe Integration Test Flow
### Uses IntelliJ HTTP Client scripting (client.global.set) to auto-capture
### tokens/IDs between requests, and {{$uuid}} to auto-generate idempotency keys.
### Adjust host, login path, and field names below to match your actual API.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### =========================================================
### 0. Login — captures the JWT automatically for every request below
### =========================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test-merchant@example.com",
  "password": "your-password"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
%}


### =========================================================
### 1. HAPPY PATH — create, charge, and refund a payment
### =========================================================

### 1a. Create a payment intent — fresh idempotency key each run
# Expect: 202 Accepted, status = CREATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 129,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("paymentIntentId", response.body.id);
%}

### 1b. Process the payment intent — charges via Stripe (pm_card_visa → should SUCCEED)
# Expect: status = SUCCEEDED
# Check DB separately: payment_intents.processor_reference should now be populated
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 1c. Create a refund against the now-SUCCEEDED payment intent
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 2000
}

> {%
    client.global.set("refundId", response.body.id);
%}

### 1d. Process the refund — should SUCCEED now that processorReference exists
# Expect: status = SUCCEEDED
# Check DB separately: refunds.processor_reference should now be populated
POST {{baseUrl}}/refunds/{{refundId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### =========================================================
### 2. DECLINE PATH — force a card decline
### =========================================================
### Before running this section: temporarily swap the hardcoded test
### payment method constant in StripeProcessor from "pm_card_visa" to
### a decline-triggering test token (e.g. "pm_card_chargeDeclined"),
### rebuild, and rerun. Swap it back afterward.

### 2a. Create a fresh payment intent for the decline test
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 1500,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("declinePaymentIntentId", response.body.id);
%}

### 2b. Process it — should FAIL (Declined branch)
# Expect: status = FAILED
# Check DB separately: processor_reference should remain null
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{declinePaymentIntentId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### =========================================================
### 3. Sanity check — refund cannot exceed remaining balance
### =========================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/payment-intents/{{paymentIntentId}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amountMinorUnits": 999999
}
